<title>UK: World Bank adds 500 mln marks to zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank adds 500 mln marks to zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Paribas.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT  * 1.5 BLN DEM   COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    08.NOV.16</p>
<p> TYPE   ZERO-COUPON   ISS PRICE  28.35     PAY DATE    07.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  30 BP     REOFFER    28.15     SPREAD	-2 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    * ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 1.0 BLN DEM ON 15.OCT.96</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    10 BP     SELL CONC  20 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 2016 BUND</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
